sub_020335F4 is defined with an empty parameter list (unk_02031734.c:1718) and
called here with one argument through the unprototyped header declaration.
wasm types calls, so wasm-ld would replace the call with a trap; the ROM
passes r0=0, which the callee never reads, so dropping it is the same call.

sub_0202D9A0 (arm9/asm/unk_0202D8D0.s) returns whatever the comm command's
size callback returns (`blx r0; add r4, r0, #0; ...; add r0, r4, #0`), and
the variable-size callback sub_0202DA78 returns 0x0000FFFF. The prototype
said s16: mwcc's sub_02030C8C keeps r0 as it comes (unk_0202F150.o:
`bl sub_0202D9A0; add r4, r0, #0; ...; ldr r0, =0xFFFF; cmp r4, r0`), so
the ROM sees 0xFFFF and reads the two-byte length that follows; the typed
wasm bridge sign-extended it to -1, `r4 == 0xffff` failed and the packet was
taken as having size -1. The prototype now says u32, the width the assembly
returns (an unknown of pc/tools/dp_retwidth_lint.py, reviewed by hand: the
lint cannot follow the callback table).

UNK_021C59F4 (u8) and UNK_021C59F8 (the comm system pointer) are adjacent
in the ROM's .bss, and the asm bodies of sub_02030674 / sub_0202FE2C reach
the pointer as [UNK_021C59F4 + 4]. clang placed them 2 bytes apart, so on a
boot with a save the main menu's comm poll read a wild pointer from F4+4
(SIGBUS in sub_02030674 at ~frame 1560). They are now one object laid out
as the ROM has them (pc/tools/dp_adjacency_lint.py finds this class).

--- a/unk_0202F150.c
+++ b/unk_0202F150.c
@@ -7,8 +7,18 @@
 #include "unk_02031480.h"
 #include "unk_02031734.h"
 
-u8 UNK_021C59F4;
-struct UnkStruct0202F150 *UNK_021C59F8;
+/* wasm: the ROM's .bss layout, which the asm bodies below rely on
+ * (sub_02030674, sub_0202FE2C: `ldr r7, =UNK_021C59F4; ldr r5, [r7, #4]`
+ * is UNK_021C59F8). One object defined under the symbol name the asm uses;
+ * the C name UNK_021C59F4 is that symbol's first byte, UNK_021C59F8 its
+ * second word. (A macro for UNK_021C59F4 would also rewrite the asm
+ * bodies' literal pools, which go through the preprocessor.) */
+extern u8 UNK_021C59F4;
+struct {
+    u8 unk021C59F4;
+    struct UnkStruct0202F150 *unk021C59F8;
+} sUnk021C59F4 __asm__("UNK_021C59F4");
+#define UNK_021C59F8 (sUnk021C59F4.unk021C59F8)
 
 vu8 UNK_02105D59 = 4;
 vu8 UNK_02105D58 = 4;
@@ -36,7 +46,7 @@
